\textit{(From \cite{LWX126}, Theorem 1.3.)}

[Browder \cite{Browder}] 
   There exist framed manifolds in dimension $n$ of Kervaire invariant one if and only if
   \begin{enumerate}
       \item[(1)] $n=2^{j+1}-2$, and
       \item[(2)] the element $h_j^2$ in the Adams spectral sequence survives to the $E_\infty$-page.
   \end{enumerate}
